<!--
    angr Phoenix short-circuit condition folding across a NON-TRIVIAL sibling
    block (`_match_acyclic_short_circuit_conditions` + the
    `MultiStatementExpression` relaxation, phoenix.py:2688), S8 "goto-quality"
    sub-stage.  Closes proposal issue angr-tr-build-spec-list.

    THE GAP.  Both of kuna's structurers implement Ghidra's `ruleBlockOr`
    short-circuit schema, which declines the `A || B` fold whenever the SIBLING
    condition block is *complex* (`BlockBasic::isComplex`, block.cc:2403: more
    than two statements).  One spill or address computation parked in front of
    the second test is enough to decline it, and kuna then emits the second
    condition as its own block that jumps back into the first arm's clause: a
    crossing goto where angr emits one compound condition.  On coreutils
    tr::build_spec_list that is literally

        result_idx = &v10;
        if (es_match(es,v12,'=')) goto label_40242e;

    THE OPTION.  `option condfold off|on|wide` (default OFF, ELEM 4113) adds a
    second disjunct at that single decline, whose admission predicate is the
    UNION of two rules.  This witness exercises Rule A (bounded prefix, from
    PR #193): a complex sibling is accepted when it is a BlockCopy of ONE basic
    block whose printed prefix is bounded (<=1 statement-root call; <=5
    statements at `on`, angr's own threshold, <=9 at `wide`), branch-free, and
    comment-free.  Rule A is tried first and is the disjunct that fires here
    (traced with KUNA_CONDFOLD_DEBUG=1).  Rule B (the statement-shape allowlist,
    from PR #194) is exercised end to end by the companion witness
    tests/stages/ghangr-condfold-newbury.xml, which needs Rule B's nested
    BlockCondition operand to fold a guard cascade; the two rules are isolated
    from each other by the unit tests in p8_structure/blockaction/tests.rs.
    The prefix then renders
    inside the AND/OR operand as a C comma expression, which the printer
    already supports (comma_separate).  No p-code is moved, cloned, or deleted:
    the fold re-parents two existing structuring nodes, and C's short-circuit
    plus comma sequencing preserves the original execution paths and order.

    THE WITNESS (self-contained, no relocations, no calls).  A function with
    exactly the schema shape:

        cf:      test edi,edi ; jne SHARED        <- bl   (the first condition)
        SIB:     mov [g1],rdx ; mov [g2],edi      <- the prefix that makes the
                 test esi,esi ; jne SHARED           sibling *complex*
        OTHER:   cmp esi,3 ; jg ... ; ret
        SHARED:  mov [g1],rsi ; cmp edi,10 ; jl OTHER ; ret

    SHARED is reached from both `cf` and SIB and itself branches back to OTHER,
    so with the fold declined the structurer must cut a goto.

    PASS 1 (`option condfold off`) = the bug: two nested ifs and a crossing
    `goto label_401019` back out of the first arm.
    PASS 2 (`option condfold on`) = the fix: one compound condition carrying the
    sibling's prefix as a comma expression, and the goto/label pair is gone.

    Asserts are counted across BOTH passes, so a token that appears once per
    pass asserts min=max=2 and a token unique to one pass asserts min=max=1.
-->
